  "instance_name": "anti_nazi_german_women",
  "label": "Anti-Nazi German Women",
  "description": "German women who opposed the Nazi regime during World War II. Many were persecuted, imprisoned, or murdered by the Nazis for their resistance activities. The claim in the meme that their bones are still in the ovens is factually inaccurate and misleading. The crematorium at Buchenwald was used for the mass cremation of murdered prisoners, not for the remains of anti-Nazi women, who were typically executed or died in other ways.",
